Thanks @robowen1 — that's exactly the evidence this PR was missing, and the cache-size delta (142M → 344M) is a much better signal than the hash assertions alone.

On your last point: agreed, keying on the full zero-limit modality set is slightly stricter than `supports_multimodal_inputs()` strictly requires. I kept it at that granularity deliberately, to match `language_model_only` — an extra recompile is the safe direction, and a narrower key would have to re-derive the "all modalities zero" condition in a second place.

@vllm-project maintainers: CI here is blocked at `pre-run-check` (the ready-label / merged-PR gate), so `pre-commit` and the test suite are all `SKIPPED` and nothing has actually run. Could someone add the `ready` label so the checks can execute? The regression is a hard startup crash with AOT compile enabled, and it now has independent end-to-end confirmation from the original reporter on the hardware that produced it.

